  "description": "Learn essential Chinese greetings and polite expressions to start any conversation with confidence.",
  "guidebook": "## Greetings in Chinese 🇨🇳\n\nChinese greetings are wonderfully simple! The most common hello is **你好** (nǐ hǎo), used in most situations. For a polite version, use **您好** (nín hǎo) when addressing elders or strangers.\n\n**Good morning** is **早上好** (zǎoshang hǎo), **good evening** is **晚上好** (wǎnshang hǎo), and **good night** is **晚安** (wǎn'ān).\n\n**Goodbye** has several forms: **再见** (zàijiàn) is standard, while **拜拜** (bàibài) is a casual borrowed form from English \"bye-bye.\"\n\n**Politeness matters!** Always say **请** (qǐng) for \"please\" and **谢谢** (xièxie) for \"thank you.\" A polite **不客气** (bú kèqi) means \"you're welcome.\"\n\n**How are you?** is **你好吗？** (nǐ hǎo ma?) — the particle **吗** turns a statement into a yes/no question. A common reply is **我很好** (wǒ hěn hǎo), \"I'm very well.\"\n\n**Tip:** Chinese often drops pronouns, so **好** alone can mean \"okay\" or \"good!\"",
